A method that declares T and returns *T could produce a pointer to any
requested type. Since plumb can also dereference that pointer, the method could
satisfy any request for a value. Reject it as for a generic function that
returns *T.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrBareTypeParamResult
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type Factory struct{}

//plumb:build
func (Factory) Make[T any]() *T { return new(T) }
